WEBVTT

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.830
How was I, Father?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.780
You were wonderful.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.870
I'm looking forward to next month's
All-Federation String Recital.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.750
Master.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.940
You have a visitor.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.180
I knew it. It's the Colonel!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.940
Do you like it?

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.960
Very much. It's quite delicious.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.280
Like he could've said no!

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.200
Father!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.430
Oh yes, I hear you've been frequenting
the mess hall these days, Colonel Ios.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.900
Is it because of some lady friend?

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.810
Is it?

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.420
N-No, of course not!

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.220
I just enjoy being able to talk with my men.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.720
Calm down. I was just kidding.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.420
Is that so?

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.000
So the situation on the front lines is grim.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.680
If Krisna manages to ally with Orlando,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.730
they'll become our biggest threat.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.310
I sympathize with Secretary General Loquis.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:39.530
Secretary General Loquis has sought your
reinstatement more fervently than anyone.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:43.480
Additionally, he's aware of your heroic
deeds during the siege of Assam Castle.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:49.210
He also testified to your innocence
during your Federal Court Marshall.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.340
And at the same time, he has transferred full
command of the Krisnan subjugation forces to you...

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.750
...General Borcuse.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:01.950
Understood.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.750
I will topple Krisna.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.000
Father.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.130
Colonel.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.560
You're leaving for the battlefield again, aren't you...

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.730
Sorrow's just part of life.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.400
I'll return unharmed like I always do.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.590
So don't you worry, Leda.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.860
I'll be there for your recital.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.330
Along with the Colonel, of course.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.870
Isn't that right, Colonel?

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:29.400
Yes, sir!

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.010
Colonel, how's my Hycherion?

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:50.350
We figured out a way to transport it
and sent it to Irios for further repairs.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:51.980
And my men?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.770
They're assembling in Irios.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.770
Excellent.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.010
Ow!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.740
Why you little...

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.730
You little turd! You think I can't reach you up there?

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.380
Hey! How long are you gonna keep picking on him?!

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.710
It's only natural for the prey to be killed by the predator.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:08.460
Huh?

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.530
Just let it go.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.260
But he's toying with him!

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.290
Quit arguing and give me a hand here, you heartless jerk!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.480
I will not let you use me as a stepping stool.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.880
No matter what.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:28.810
I <i>told</i> you, you could stand on top of my back.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.510
Hi guys! Pleasure to meet you.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.850
You can use my back if you'd like.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.470
You're a pretty generous guy. Unlike this grouch.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.410
My name's Rygart. Who're you?

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.530
The name's Hodr.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.370
Nice to meet you, Hodr.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.810
Alright then. I'll take my shoes off.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.730
It's alright. I don't mind.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.760
I was about to give this uniform a much-needed washing anyway.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.790
Sorry. Would you rather I piggybacked instead?

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.660
Nah. That would be rather
awkward for both of us, so no thanks.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.740
You ready?

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:02.340
Yeah.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.630
Don't you dare!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.930
Hey, that's a baby Black Owl.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:15.920
He'll slowly start turning black.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.990
You sure know your birds.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:18.860
Rygart.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.270
Yeah?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.920
The man you just stepped on is the
heir to the throne of your nation.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.710
What did he just...

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.620
Y-Your Majesty, I offer you this
bird and beg for your forgiveness.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.960
Unbelievable. You don't even know your own King's name.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.320
Just shut up.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:48.320
If you will acknowledge the above,
swear loyalty to King Krisna IX,

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:54.220
and to protect the lives and wealth of the
citizens all in the name of the Lævateinn,

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.580
step forward.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:07:02.250
Secondary Heavy-Knight number 1728, Rygart Arrow.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:07.220
Protect Krisna under General Baldr as the primary pilot

00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:12.730
and secondary person in charge of the Under Golem.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:17.090
Kneel and accept the Lævateinn as proof of a heavy knight.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.790
Hey, get on your knees.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.680
No, it's fine.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.830
Give it to me.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:32.700
But, the ritual's...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.480
You're...

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.610
an idiot.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.970
I know, stupid.

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.570
Hey, hey, hey...

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:18.430
Can he fight with something that heavy?

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.700
It's totally mysterious as to why he can even walk.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.440
The Under Golem shall receive the name Delphing.

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:30.670
Zess...

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.110
<i>I'm going to protect Hodr's kingdom.</i>

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:43.930
Zess! You know the conditions for surrender, right?

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.580
<i>The conditions?</i>

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.170
<i>There are two conditions.</i>

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.090
<i>Both of which involve the vested
privileges of the royal family.</i>

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.080
<i>Hodr is a generous king.</i>

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.970
<i>He even risked causing conflict among the nobles
over allowing ordinary citizens to hold office.</i>

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.630
<i>The terms should be more than reasonable.</i>

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:06.350
<i>Is there something else to this?</i>

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:09.840
<i>Why did you get involved, Rygart?</i>

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.370
<i>He should be well aware of our military's power.</i>

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:19.410
<i>Why won't you just surrender, Hodr?</i>

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:51.110
Judging from our remaining ammunition stores,
we can afford to fight one more battle.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.690
Shall we proceed as planned?

00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:58.440
Yeah. We'll make a third strike on Binonten,
then retreat to the border.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.370
Cleo...

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.550
Do you feel alright?

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.450
Yes, sir. I'm okay.

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:10.430
Cleo.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.280
During the Krisnan war of independence,
they slaughtered civilians near the borders,

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.860
hacked off the limbs of our
captured soldiers and sent them to us.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:24.250
Now they're building favor with Orlando and
threatening this continent's peace once again.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:27.290
They are savage, despicable people.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:29.230
I'll fight them until I draw my last breath.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:38.360
<i>Lee told me not to bring my emotions into battle,
but I will bring down the Black Golem.</i>

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.240
I'll take over night watch duties. Please rest assured.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.170
I-I said I'm fine!

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.500
I never said anything...

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:56.800
History lessons sure have
changed from when I was in school.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.820
I was taught the same things as her.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.380
History books are rewritten with the changing of the times, after all.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:09.140
At any rate, classroom lectures are worlds apart from the battlefield.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.780
Pay attention, Rygart.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:24.730
This multi-layer armor was made from
leftover medium-strength armor plates.

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:29.950
While it's equipped, the Delphine's combat
capabilities are reduced by 80 percent.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.640
By gripping the lever tightly, you can disengage the armor.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.180
Just watch your timing.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.370
Also, about that strange display.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.770
Oh, you mean this one?

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.970
When the red bar reaches the end, you'll be rendered immobile.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:46.180
And it requires approximately 24 hours to recover functionality.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.440
The operational time limit for strenuous use is roughly...

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:54.940
How long?

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:55.970
Huh?

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:56.760
How much time?

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.930
Between ten and thirty minutes.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.610
I don't really believe you have the capacity to kill though.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.380
I've already killed two people.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:13.160
You're mistaken.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.780
It's not as if you yourself took their lives.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.030
No, I'm not wrong.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:24.350
Back then, I wanted the enemy to die from the bottom of my heart.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:29.870
Or else I'd wind up dead instead.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:32.820
What if you were fighting Zess?

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.390
Huh?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.100
Could you fight him with that same mentality?

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.730
Zess... There's no way I could beat him.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:45.520
There isn't a single man capable of beating him.

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.850
Zess! Zess!

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:56.160
The drill instructors would wail on
students in mock battles to blow off steam.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.640
But even a team of four instructors couldn't defeat Zess.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:16.670
Rygart.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.750
One of our scouts has informed us of the enemy's movements.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.780
We're commencing the operation. Are you ready to go?

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.730
All set.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.310
Let me say this for your own good.

00:13:28.310 --> 00:13:31.610
It is far more difficult to capture an enemy than it is to kill them.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:36.280
Capturing a soldier involves three times
the effort and three times the danger.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:39.650
If you wish to save the life of an enemy soldier,

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:41.950
remember that you'll lose three of your own in the process.

00:13:44.430 --> 00:13:45.630
That's all I wanted to say.

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:01.380
Delphine, commence operation.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:02.790
Ready to sortie.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:06.400
Just stay out of General Baldr's way, Un-sorcerer!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.040
Queen Sigyn, please stand back!

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.020
Pick up the pace, Cleo!

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:33.610
Yes, sir!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.100
Stealth isn't necessary from this point.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.530
Don't worry about leaving footprints!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:40.950
Affirmative!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:42.440
Cleo...

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.190
Yes, Captain Zess?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.620
Have you been sweeping twice to hide your steps so far?

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:48.720
Y-Yes...

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:52.650
You idiot! Southern Krisna's soil is softer!

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:55.090
Didn't I tell you to sweep at least three times?!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:16.980
<i>We're trapped!</i>

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.130
We're surrounded by enemy forces!

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.800
Abort mission! We're retreating!

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.480
There's an opening at 7 o'clock.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.050
Erekt! Secure our escape route!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.730
I-I'm sorry!

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:30.400
This isn't necessarily your fault, Cleo.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.800
Anyway, let's get moving!

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.660
Argath and I will guard the rear!

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:34.500
Sir!

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.370
Let's go, Cleo!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.240
Yes, sir!

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.320
General Baldr, the enemy's retreating!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.610
They figured it out already?!

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:49.180
Earlier than I anticipated.
Regardless, all units commence attack!

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:05.930
Cleo!

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:14.010
I'll buy some time! Go help Cleo!

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:24.880
Two kills already?!

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:26.630
He's so fast!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.230
The Killer Golem is here!

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:33.710
Damn you! Are you saying our
ambush forces aren't worth your time?

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:39.950
You're too focused on Captain Zess!

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.540
Can you move, Cleo?

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:47.540
I'm alright.

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.300
They're closing in on us...

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.450
Okay, let's move!

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.330
Looks like we managed to break free.

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.210
Badlands...

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.980
We'll regroup at point nine.

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:06.830
Roger!

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:42.940
What the hell <i>is</i> that?!

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.010
<i>Two... three... four... enemy units.</i>

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:50.180
<i>How should I handle this?</i>

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.570
If you wish to save the life of an enemy soldier...

00:17:57.170 --> 00:18:00.970
Captain Zess, let me defend the rear!

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:04.050
What the hell?!

00:18:08.300 --> 00:18:10.840
Fall back, Argath! Do not engage him!

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.010
You'll get yourself killed!

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:33.270
He's dead... He's dead, right?

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.730
Don't take it personally.

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:38.660
The fact that you're here means
you feel somewhat responsible...

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.330
Me, responsible?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.110
I don't blame myself one bit!

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.620
I never even saw Dan's face!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:48.630
Everyone, scatter!

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:07.130
Captain, please retreat!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:13.910
I'll break through that armor.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:16.150
Cleo, give him cover fire!

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:16.470
Sir!

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.470
Shoot, Cleo!

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.420
Roger!

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:31.050
<i>It's like a fortress is charging right at us!</i>

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.700
This guy hurts.

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.490
It must be Zess.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.630
Shit, he's concentrating his fire.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:45.650
He's trying to tear off my armor...

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.130
It can't take much more!

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:53.880
I'm out?!

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.650
What ridiculous height!

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.490
Captain Zess!

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:16.950
Rygart!

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.900
Get back, Erekt!

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.410
He moves so fast...

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.660
That's him!

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:37.550
Erekt...

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.500
Yeah, it's him alright. The Black Golem!

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.750
The Black Golem?!

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.120
Zess!

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:46.460
Rygart!

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:50.910
<i>If I destroy his rifle, I can save him!</i>

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:07.730
<i>Alright!</i>

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:11.700
<i>Once you get away from the Captain,
I'll turn you into a beehive, Black Golem!</i>

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.240
<i>How could I have done something so stupid?</i>

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.030
<i>I held back because I was fighting Zess.</i>

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:21.310
<i>If I don't do something, they'll waste me the second I land!</i>

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:26.200
<i>If Rygart gets too far away, Erekt and Cleo will kill him!</i>

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.180
<i>I have to be the one to do it!</i>

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.860
Rygart!

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:52.860
She's supposed to be 12?!

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:55.230
What's going on in Athens?!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.910
Whirlwind, storm and stress.
